QE Studio
=========

QE Studio's own source code has no license chosen yet (see README.md). This file lists material
from third parties that is included in, or downloaded by, QE Studio, and the terms it comes with.


1. Material included in this repository
---------------------------------------

backend/qestudio/data/qe_schema.json
    Generated by backend/tools/gen_schema.py from the PWgui module files distributed with
    Quantum ESPRESSO 7.6 (share/GUI/PWgui/modules/*), which embed the official input
    documentation (INPUT_PW, INPUT_PH, INPUT_PP, INPUT_DOS, INPUT_PROJWFC, INPUT_BANDS, INPUT_HP,
    INPUT_NEB). Variable names, labels and descriptions are taken from those files.
    PWgui: Copyright (C) 2003-2008 Anton Kokalj. Input documentation: the Quantum ESPRESSO
    developers. Both are distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at
    your option) any later version (statement in PWgui's README/COPYRIGHT). Distributing this
    file therefore requires compliance with the GPL; take this into account when choosing a
    license for QE Studio.

backend/tests/data/*
    Output files produced by Quantum ESPRESSO 7.6 (conda-forge build) for silicon, used as test
    fixtures. The pseudopotentials used to produce them were generated locally with ld1.x for
    testing only and are not distributed.

frontend/src/lib/elements.ts
    Element symbols, masses, covalent radii (Cordero et al., Dalton Trans. 2008, 2832) and Jmol
    colours, generated from ase.data (ASE, LGPL-2.1-or-later).


2. Data downloaded at the user's request
----------------------------------------

SSSP 1.3.0 pseudopotential libraries (Pseudopotentials page)
    Materials Cloud Archive record 2023.65, doi:10.24435/materialscloud:f3-ym, licensed CC BY 4.0
    according to the record page. Cite G. Prandini, A. Marrazzo, I. E. Castelli, N. Mounet and
    N. Marzari, npj Comput. Mater. 4, 72 (2018), and the original reference of each
    pseudopotential you use.

Quantum ESPRESSO executables (Connections & QE page)
    Installed from conda-forge (package "qe") with micromamba, or from the system package
    manager. Quantum ESPRESSO is free software under the GNU GPL (the conda-forge package
    metadata states GPL-2.0-only). micromamba: BSD-3-Clause (mamba-org).

Crystal structures from the Crystallography Open Database (Structures ▸ Import)
    https://www.crystallography.net/cod/ - see the COD terms of use; cite the original
    publication of each structure.


